Z||000060||EdsB52||08-12-2001||06:05 AM||||EdsB52A month ago or so a squirrel with the moniker sjp777 got extremely hostile with me, sent me threats through private email, then rescinded and said he would never write to me again. Well, I knew he couldn't stay away. It's also predictably fitting that he would hide behind the moniker of a girl, seeing that he's such a little ***** . In the following transcribed posts I will both convincingly explain why the person posting under the moniker 'FieroBritney' is a guy, and why that guy is the same person posting as sjp777. I will support this argument through the common coincidence of both monikers being present on the same thread, and the masculine language use and subject matter. I will further support this argument with the given evidence that sjp777 is from the Vancouver, Washington area, and FieroBritney posted information regarding a Fiero event in Richland, Washington which is 206 miles from the former (per mapquest). And finally, the contempt for me that is shown in the writings of sjp777 is also present in the writings of FieroBritney.<BR> <P><A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum6/HTML/002129.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum6/HTML/002129.html</A> <BR>sjp777 originates post with<BR>"Total confidence, total domination. They could really be the first team to go undefeated in the playoffs.<BR>L.A. now has what Chicago had a couple years ago. Common denominator: Phil Jackson. Yeah, I know the arguement, look at the players he's had. But what other coach can get superstar egos like that to play together as a team? All the bickering between Kobe and Shaq, just like Michael and Scotty in years past. What happens when playoff time rolls around? Egos get put aside and the ass kickin begins.<BR>cadaver replies with:<BR>"Ok time to make some more friends. <BR>You do realize that it is only a basketball game, right?"<BR>FieroBritney posts:<BR>You do realize you're being a complete dick for no reason right?"<BR>Coincidental how FieroBritney backs sjp777, isn’t it?<BR> <P><A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum2/HTML/010810.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum2/HTML/010810.html</A> <BR>Posted by FieroBritney<BR>"and I thought I had blood in MY underwear"<BR>Same thread posted by sjp777<BR>"Yes welcome. We can always use more girls in here"<BR>Same thread posted by FieroBritney<BR>"I don't know what you're talking about.<BR>How rude<BR>Why do men always think they are such know it alls"<BR>Coincidental how sjp777 backs FieroBritney, isn’t it? Would a girl in this club post like that? I think not, that’s guy talk. But yes sjp777, I’m sure you do have blood in your underwear.<BR> <P><A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum2/HTML/011485.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum2/HTML/011485.html</A> <BR>Posted by FieroBritney (really sounds like something a chick would write, doesn't it?):<BR>"Switch from a 4 speed to an auto? Are you stoned?<BR>Most people usually want to go the other way.<BR>Stick with what you have or you'll be kicking yourself afterward"<BR>Then she posted:<BR>"Fieros are sports cars. Sports cars are made to be driven, not to just point and go.<BR>Automatic Corvettes are an abomination.<BR>Automatics belong in minivans"<BR>A girl writing this? Most girls like automatics.<BR> <P><A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum2/HTML/011486.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum2/HTML/011486.html</A> <BR>FieroBritney originated this post with:<BR>"I'm running mobil 1 5w30 in my 5 speed and it seems to shift a little notchy and it's easy to blow shifts under hard acceleration.<BR>Is that oil too thin for the synchronisers to work correctly? And if so what would be better? I want to stick with a synthetic<BR>I saw some mobil 1 gear oil in the store but it was really a heavy weight and about $8 a quart. Would that work better and be worth the expense?"<BR>Then replied with:<BR>"I got the GM synchromesh.<BR>$15 a quart!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!<BR>And contrary to one of the above posts, the getrag 5 speed takes 2 quarts not 1.<BR>It had better be worth it."<BR>Then sjp777 pipes in with this affirmation of what FieroBritney wrote:<BR>"According to the chilton manual, and the original 88 fiero owners manual, the getrag takes 4 pts which is 2 quarts.<BR>The Izuzu 5 speed takes 2.7"<BR>Then FieroBritney replies with:<BR>"Update:<BR>Been 3 days with the synchromesh and so far it's very impressive. No blown shifts, no problems getting into 1st at stoplights.<BR>It's like a whole new trans. Shifts are solid and precise.<BR>2 thumbs up!"<BR>Girls racing and blowing shifts? Without being sexist, as some girls do race, it’s unusual and unlikely. Worried about synchronizers, a girl? Don’t think so. Then she straightens out the quantity issue, while sjp77 pipes in to reaffirm. ‘Shifts are solid and precise?’ Maybe Shirley Muldowny, but not the average girl in PFF.<BR> <P><A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum2/HTML/012089.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum2/HTML/012089.html</A> <BR>FieroBritney replies to an inquiry with:<BR>"Fierostore has cross drilled roters with carbomet pads for the 88's for $220 a pair.<BR>That's only about $75 more than new stock stuff and should be plenty worth the added expense.”<BR>Girls worrying about the brake rotors for maximum braking and concerned with the pad composition? Doesn’t wash.<BR> <P><A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum2/HTML/012184.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum2/HTML/012184.html</A> <BR>FieroBritney replies to an inquiry with:<BR>"Just ask a dealer for GTA hood louvers from a late 80's trans am. They are still available new from pontiac and cost $35 each. If your dealer doesn't have them in stock, he can easily order them."<BR>More stuff on technical information.<BR> <P><A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum1/HTML/007713.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum1/HTML/007713.html</A> <BR>sjp777 initiates a thread with:<BR>"Even though I despise George W, with the passage of his tax plan we all get rebates this year.<BR>$300 for singles, $500 for single parents, and $600 for married couples.<BR>We should all have our checks by September. I will be buying a kevlar clutch from Fierostore if my current one lasts until I get the check. If I have to replace it on my own before that, I will be calling Mr Mike for some leather seats when the check arrives.<BR>What FIERO RELATED things will you all be doing with the extra cash?"<BR>Sjp777 replies to LZeitgeist with:<BR>"Get out from under your car once and awhile."<BR>Sjp777 posts:<BR>"always a few Doubting Thomas'<BR>If you pay income tax, you'll get it. I'm sure Mr Bush will see to it that you do. Now that the democrats control congress again (thank you God), it's probably that last bit of his original agenda that will see the light of day."<BR>FieroBritney posts:<BR>"Stop, you'll jinx it!<BR>I need a new dress to go with my new name.<BR>some shoes would be nice too"<BR>This one is interesting. FieroBritney supports sjp777, but gives herself away with the new name remark. But yes sjp777, I’m sure you can buy a new dress and shoes. They’ll probably go well with your slight disposition and tendency toward effeminate behavior.<BR>  <P><A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum1/HTML/007721.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum1/HTML/007721.html</A> <BR>FieroBritney replies to a post regarding changing user name:<BR>"so there"<BR>Right, confirmation and a little sass.<BR> <P><A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum1/HTML/008338.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum1/HTML/008338.html</A> <BR>FieroBritney posts a resource in regard to engine modification: <A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/fiero88gt1/top_ten_budget_fiero_enhancement.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://www.geocities.com/fiero88gt1/top_ten_budget_fiero_enhancement.htm</A> <BR>More of the same. A supposed girl posting information on engine enhancements and oil viscosities; highly unlikely.<BR> <P><A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum1/HTML/008842.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum1/HTML/008842.html</A> <BR>FieroBritney posts a Fiero event in Washington. How coincidental, sjp777 lives a couple hundred miles from there:<BR>"Pasted below are the details. I hope it formats ok. It's too much to retype.<BR>NORTHWEST FIERO FEST 2001 <BR>RICHLAND, WASHINGTON, AUGUST 10, 11, 12 <P>SCHEDULE OF EVENTS <BR>FRIDAY EVENING, AUG. 10TH: Pick up your " goodie bag " and event info, and enjoy a light meal and beverages on the lawn next to the Columbia River. 7:00 til 9:00 PM <BR>SATURDAY MORNING, AUG. 11TH: Show lot opens at 8:00 at McCurley Pontiac in Pasco. McCurley is providing wash and detail bays, first come, first serve. Judging begins at 11:00 AM sharp. Show ends at 2:00 PM. <BR>SATURDAY EVENING: Banquet and awards at the Tower Inn in Richland. After the banquet, we will go on a 11 mile cruise on George Washington Drive with the assistance of the local law enforcement. <BR>SUNDAY MORNING, AUG. 12TH: Breakfast with friends, then out to the back lot at 9;00 AM for " slow drags, and the infamous " bean bag toss". About 12:00 noon we will say farewell til next year. <P>REGISTRATION INFORMATION <BR>CLASSIFICATIONS <BR>A. 84 Stock coupe/SE B. 84 Stock Indy Pace Car C. 85 Stock coupe/ SE D. 85 Stock GT <BR>B. E. 86 Stock coupe/SE F. 86 Stock GT G. 87 Stock coupe/SE H. 87 Stock GT I. 88 Stock coupe <BR>C. J. 88 Stock Formula K. 88 Stock GT L. Mera/Zimmer M.Custom N.Custom Modified <BR>D. O.Super Modified P.Kit Car Q. Concours ( 2000 miles or less for each year of existence, any model ) <P>REGISTRATION DUE BY JULY, 20. AFTER THAT ADD $ 10.00 <BR>Registration fee.................................... $ 35.00 <BR>Late fee................................................ ______ <BR>Friday reception (per person).............. $ 5.00 <BR>Banquet (per person).......................... $ 25.00 <BR>Additional T-Shirts ( each ).................. $ 15.00 <BR>(one free with registration) <BR>Med___ Large___XL___XXL____ <BR>Additional dash plaque (one free)....... $ 3.00 <BR>Check #________ TOTAL......... $________ <P>MAKE CHECKS PAYABLE TO: PEGASUS PRODUCTIONS <BR>12530 182ND AVE. S.E. <BR>SNOHOMISH, WA. 98290 <P>CONTACT SHILO INN DIRECT FOR ROOM RESERVATIONS ( 509 ) 946-4661 <P>REGIONAL CONTACTS <BR>BOISE IDAHO: Bill Grant Fiero84@aol.com <BR>BRITISH COLUMBIA: David Bergquist Captfieroofbc@home.com <BR>PORTLAND, OREGON: Dan Tucker 17ccm@home.com <BR>RENO, NEVADA: Kym Robinson Fieroroadclub@aol.com <BR>WESTERN WASHINGTON: Ben Didlot Benjamatic@aol.com <BR>EASTERN WASHINGTON: Greg Gulliford Lilrdfiero@servershare.net <BR>HOTEL ROOM RATES <BR>1-2 PERSONS $65.00 <BR>2-4 PERSONS $75.00 <BR>Make reservations by July 9th to lock in these rates <BR>From I-82, exit on George Washington Dr. and head north"<P>Who was it that wrote those truly brilliant words; A lot of work to prove the obvious? Yes, again true on both accounts. Now sjp777 will pipe in with his anger at me bringing this up and that it’s a big lie. And in order to maintain the façade, FieroBritney will continue to post. The one question I have is that if sjp777 also goes out in public trying to pass as FieroBritney minus the Fiero, or if his cross-gendered charade starts and ends here? Sjp777, are you gender dysphoric? Actually, scratch it, I don’t want to know and please don’t post pictures.<P>Now that I’ve briefed the posts, I’m further able to cement my correlation between FieroBritney and sjp777. In his rant in this thread FieroBritney wrote:<BR>“Remember what I said about who has whom in their mouth now?” And:<BR>“Who's got whom in their mouth now? Losers.”<BR>And from private email, sjp777 wrote:<BR>“And I’m so happy to see I made your list.”<BR>Without further referring to the dark days, this is in reference to the list that was posted in which sjp777 was a member. And yes, we all know what you said about the mouth list.<BR>Then Fiero Britney wrote:<BR>“Let eds fight his own battles. He is the catylist for the negativity. Since it seems he can act with impunity, I will make it a point to act in kind. Someone will end up getting banned. Whether it's him or me, I'm beyond caring. It's all about the end result now.”<BR>Of course you don’t care if FieroBritney gets banned, that moniker is expendable. What you want to occur is for FieroBritney and EdsB52 to get banned so you can start posting again. You know, I deserve no medal of brilliance for figuring this out, as simple people leave trails of clues everywhere.<BR>FieroBritney wrote:<BR>“This forum has been seriously damaged by this assh*le. Good people have left. He has tied up many threads with his (your) bullsh*t.:<BR>Pretty insightful for someone that’s supposedly been here since May with 24 posts. It’s almost as if you’ve been here longer.<BR>FieroBritney wrote:<BR>“I am not concerned with his weak threats at intimidation.”<BR>What threats and intimidation? Please post them.<BR>FieroBritney wrote:<BR>“I've got big plans for you.”<BR>Sjp777 wrote in private email:<BR>“I am embarrassed to think you’re from Tempe. I obviously have spent a lot of time there. In fact, I’ll probably be moving back there by year-end. Maybe I’ll see you around.” “I would love to meet you though”<BR>Why be ambiguous, spell out your big plans or continue to be thought of as a no-show. I mean, it seems like you’re right on the brink of making some great declaration, so please do. I’ll tell you what, you talk and I’ll listen (an offer most would jump at!).<p>[This message has been edited by EdsB52 (edited 08-12-2001).]||||reg||1
